commit 4bd3f760c3c3ffa81efebabb8dd29611925b6b97
Author: Devuser <hi@devuser.nu>
Date:   Sat Jul 11 22:27:03 2026 +0200

    feat(feed)!: contract v3 cutover, refs-only article identity everywhere

    Numeric article ids (articleId/article_id/id) never gave callers anything article_ref didn't already carry more durably, so the boundary is refs-only now: every feedq command stamps schemaVersion 3, articles/coverage/live/status projections drop the numeric fields, and feedq.schema.json rejects a stale v2 payload instead of silently accepting half-migrated rows. articles --id becomes --ref (article_ref or source URL) so a stale caller gets an actionable error, not a wrong result. The pipeline articles adapter already relayed only article_ref/revision, so it just drops the now-impossible legacy field declarations to match.

